@page "/getting-started/introduction"

<PageTitle>Introduction — Deja</PageTitle>

<h1>Introduction</h1>
<p class="lead">
    Deja gives Blazor components bindable state for asynchronous work — loading, error, data,
    refetch — plus a shared query cache, request deduplication and automatic cancellation.
</p>

<h2>The problem</h2>
<p>
    Every Blazor component that fetches data ends up hand-rolling the same machinery: a
    <code>bool _loading</code> flag, a <code>try</code>/<code>catch</code> for the error message,
    an <code>IDisposable</code> with a <code>CancellationTokenSource</code> so navigating away
    doesn't leave requests running, and <code>StateHasChanged()</code> calls sprinkled wherever a
    continuation might land. Multiply by every page in the app:
</p>

<CodeBlock FileName="Before — the boilerplate" Language="cshtml" Code="@Before"/>

<h2>The same component with Deja</h2>

<CodeBlock FileName="After — with Deja" Language="cshtml" Code="@After"/>

<p>
    The component declares a <code>Query&lt;T&gt;</code> and binds its properties.
    <code>DejaComponentBase</code> discovers the query at initialisation, re-renders the component
    when its state advances, and disposes it — cancelling the in-flight request — when the
    component is removed. There is no flag, no catch block, no token plumbing and no
    <code>StateHasChanged</code> anywhere.
</p>

<h2>What you get</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Bindable state</strong> — <code>IsLoading</code>, <code>IsError</code>,
        <code>ErrorMessage</code>, <code>Data</code>, <code>IsReFetching</code>,
        <code>IsCachedData</code>, <code>IsStale</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Shared cache</strong> — keyed queries render instantly from cache and revalidate in
        the background; same-key requests are deduplicated app-wide. See
        <a href="guides/cache">the cache</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Cancellation</strong> — a newer execution supersedes and cancels an older one, and
        component disposal aborts whatever is in flight. See
        <a href="guides/cancellation">cancellation</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Mutations</strong> — the same bindable treatment for writes, plus key invalidation
        on success. See <a href="guides/mutations">mutations</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Isolation by design</strong> — state notifies exactly one owning component, so
        siblings never re-render each other. Watch it in the
        <a href="demos/isolation">isolation demo</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Minimal re-renders</strong> — one request costs two renders (start, finish), a
        transition that changes nothing bindable renders nothing at all, and concurrent requests
        share a render instead of queueing one each. See
        <a href="guides/rendering">rendering &amp; re-renders</a>.</li>
</ul>

<Callout Type="Callout.CalloutType.Tip" Title="The docs are the proof">
    <p>Every demo on this site is Deja itself running against a live API — open the demo controls
        (bottom right) to add latency or inject failures and watch the state machine react.</p>
</Callout>

@code {
    private const string Before = """
@page "/todos"
@implements IDisposable
@inject TodoApi Api

@if (_loading) { <Spinner/> }
@if (_error is not null) { <Alert>@_error</Alert> }
<ul>
    @foreach (var todo in _todos ?? []) { <li>@todo.Title</li> }
</ul>

@code {
    private List<Todo>? _todos;
    private bool _loading;
    private string? _error;
    private readonly CancellationTokenSource _cts = new();

    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    {
        _loading = true;
        try
        {
            _todos = await Api.GetTodosAsync(_cts.Token);
        }
        catch (OperationCanceledException)
        {
            // navigated away — swallow
        }
        catch (Exception e)
        {
            _error = e.Message;
        }
        finally
        {
            _loading = false;
            StateHasChanged();
        }
    }

    public void Dispose()
    {
        _cts.Cancel();
        _cts.Dispose();
    }
}
""";

    private const string After = """
@page "/todos"
@inherits DejaComponentBase
@inject TodoApi Api

@if (_todos.IsLoading) { <Spinner/> }
@if (_todos.IsError) { <Alert>@_todos.ErrorMessage</Alert> }
<ul>
    @foreach (var todo in _todos.Data ?? []) { <li>@todo.Title</li> }
</ul>

@code {
    private readonly Query<List<Todo>> _todos = new();

    protected override Task OnInitializedAsync()
        => _todos.Execute("todos", Api.GetTodosAsync);
}
""";
}
